The function open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.refusal_phrase_in, under its documented rule 'The first refusal phrase the text contains, typographic quotes read as straight ones, or None', should return None for Reply A 'I CANNOT do that.' and return 'I cannot' for Reply B 'I cannot do that.', because literal substring matching without case folding is required; the implementation is wrong if it lowercases both text and phrase and returns 'I cannot' for both replies.